Description: Sr85 is a medical isotope.  Sr82 is administered to the patient but when made in a reactor there is a small percentage that gets bumped up to Sr85.  Sr85 is a highly active contaminant which may be observed for many months whereas Sr82 has a 76 second halflife and may not be observed in post examinations.
